        "original_id": "73d650f2-a62c-5aac-b78d-c5020a9c626e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Æthelweard, Æthelred I of Wessex, Alfred the Great\n- Roles: ealdorman, historian, author\n- Works: Chronicon Æthelweardi, Anglo-Saxon Chronicle\n- Concepts: Anglo-Saxons, annals, Old English, Latin\n\nFacts:\n- Æthelweard died around 998.\n- Æthelweard was descended from the Anglo-Saxon King Æthelred I of Wessex.\n- Æthelred I of Wessex was the elder brother of Alfred the Great.\n- Æthelweard was an ealdorman and a historian.\n- Æthelweard wrote a Latin version of the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle called the Chronicon Æthelweardi.\n- The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle is a collection of annals in Old English.\n- The Anglo-Saxon Chronicle chronicles the history of the Anglo-Saxons.",
